<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>How blinded we have been:</l><l>“We’ll build Your habitation”</l><l>When we are short of Christ—</l><l>We need Your saturation!</l><l>O Lord, You care for our house!</l><l>Oh, what a blessed word!</l><l>As You’re to God, You’d be to us—</l><l>A mutual abode.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>There’s nothing that we are</l><l>Or have or do well-pleasing;</l><l>We need Thee, glorious Christ,</l><l>Inwrought into our being.</l><l>O Lord, our heart’s still vacant now!</l><l>Come in and settle down.</l><l>Come saturate and permeate</l><l>And fill us with Yourself.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Our spirit You have filled</l><l>At our regeneration,</l><l>But mind, emotion, will</l><l>Await Your saturation.</l><l>How much of You is built in us</l><l>To make our heart Your home?</l><l>O Triune God, we welcome You.</l><l>Come build, oh, build in us.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Into our innermost</l><l>Intrinsic constitution,</l><l>Come, Lord, Yourself dispense</l><l>By constant, fresh infusion;</l><l>Transform us, Lord, and work Yourself,</l><l>As God’s embodiment,</l><l>Into our heart, and life each part,</l><l>With Your reality.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>To build Your house today,</l><l>Self-effort You’re refusing—</l><l>All stubble, wood, and hay;</l><l>Gold, silver, gems, You’re using.</l><l>The consummated Triune God</l><l>Transmitted into us</l><l>Now builds Himself into a home—</l><l>His dwelling, glorious.</l><l>(Repeat the last four lines)</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
